      "message": "The downgrade() flips the server_default back to false but never backfills the data, unlike upgrade() which does a `WHERE overcloud IS NOT TRUE` update. A rollback leaves every existing host still holding overcloud\u003dtrue in the data while a freshly-created host defaults to false, so the column default and the stored values disagree. Add the mirror backfill (e.g. `op.execute(\"UPDATE hosts SET overcloud \u003d false WHERE overcloud IS NOT FALSE\")`) before the alter_column so downgrade is the clean inverse.",
